[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"JavaScript Inheritance with 'extends'"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Inheritance is a fundamental concept in object-oriented programming (OOP) that allows you to create new classes based on existing classes. The new classes inherit properties and methods from the existing class, which is called the parent or base class. In JavaScript, inheritance is achieved using the 'extends' keyword in class declarations."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Basic Syntax"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"The 'extends' keyword is used in the class declaration to specify the parent class. The syntax is as follows:"},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
  constructor(args) {
    super(args);
    // Additional initialization
  }
  // Additional methods
}"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"Here, 'ChildClass' inherits from 'ParentClass'. The 'super()' method is crucial; it calls the constructor of the parent class and must be called before using 'this' in the child class's constructor."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Example: Animal and Dog Classes"},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"class Animal {
  constructor(name) {
    this.name = name;
  }

  speak() {
    console.log('Generic animal sound');
  }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
  constructor(name, breed) {
    super(name);
    this.breed = breed;
  }

  speak() {
    console.log('Woof!');
  }

  wagTail() {
    console.log('Wagging tail');
  }
}

const myDog = new Dog('Buddy', 'Golden Retriever');
myDog.speak(); // Output: Woof!
myDog.wagTail(); // Output: Wagging tail
console.log(myDog.name); // Output: Buddy"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"In this example, the 'Dog' class inherits from the 'Animal' class. The 'Dog' class has its own constructor that calls the 'Animal' class's constructor using 'super(name)'. The 'Dog' class also overrides the 'speak()' method and adds a new method 'wagTail()'."},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"The 'super()' Keyword"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"The 'super()' keyword is used to call functions on a parent object. It has two primary uses:"},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Calling the parent class's constructor: 'super(args)' in the child class's constructor initializes the parent class's properties."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Calling parent class methods: 'super.methodName(args)' allows you to invoke a method defined in the parent class from the child class."},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Method Overriding"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Method overriding occurs when a child class defines a method with the same name as a method in its parent class. The child class's method will be called instead of the parent class's method. In the 'Dog' example, the 'speak()' method is overridden."},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"Benefits of Inheritance"},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Code Reusability: Avoids duplicating code by inheriting properties and methods from parent classes."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Code Organization: Promotes a hierarchical structure, making code easier to understand and maintain."},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Polymorphism: Allows objects of different classes to be treated as objects of a common type."},{"order":20,"type":"subheading","text":"Important Considerations"},{"order":21,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always call 'super()' in the child class's constructor before using 'this'."},{"order":22,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Be mindful of the inheritance hierarchy to avoid complex and difficult-to-manage relationships."},{"order":23,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Consider composition over inheritance when appropriate to reduce coupling between classes."},{"order":24,"type":"paragraph","text":"Understanding and utilizing inheritance effectively is crucial for writing well-structured and maintainable JavaScript code."}]
